----------------------------------------------------
This is a simple assignment, to understand the overall pipeline we will follow
in our assignments. 
----------------------------------------------------
USAGE: 
1) Run "make", to get executable "main".
2) Run "./main <INPUT FILE> <OUTPUT FILE>"

Example:
./main simple-input.txt student-output.txt
./main Tests/more-input.txt student-output.txt

----------------------------------------------------
This program solves the N-Queens problem using backtracking.
It supports optional pre-placed queens given in the input file.
The goal is to place N queens on an NxN board so that no two queens
attack each other (same row, same column, or diagonal).
----------------------------------------------------

PROBLEM RULES:
A queen attacks another queen if they share:
1) the same row
2) the same column
3) the same diagonal

A solution is an arrangement of N queens where none attack each other.

----------------------------------------------------

TEST OUTPUT (Java Helper):
To view/verify an output file in a clean formatted way, a Java helper program is provided.
Go into the Helper directory, compile the helper, and run it on an output file.

Commands:
javac PrintSolutionHelper.java

Run on simple output:
java PrintSolutionHelper ../simple-output.txt

Run on more outputs:
java PrintSolutionHelper ../Tests/more-output.txt
java PrintSolutionHelper ../Tests/test-5-output.txt